{%- comment -%}
  Section divider mask — Liquid mirror of `renderMask`
  (src/components/builder/blocks/atoms/section/render.tsx), with the path data
  mirroring `sectionMasks` (src/utils/builder/schema/section-masks.ts). Keep the
  three in sync: what the canvas draws is what publishes.

  Params:
    mask_type     - mask key (`simple-waves`, …). `none` / unknown → nothing.
    mask_height   - `sm|md|lg|xl` scale step (emitted as data-mask-height, sized
                    in dm-theme.css) or a raw px number.
    mask_position - `top` | `bottom`. Paths are authored for the BOTTOM edge;
                    the top edge is their vertical mirror (`scaleY(-1)`), and
                    `rotate: true` masks carry a 180° base — mirroring
                    `maskTransform`. A `directional` motif (diagonal stripes)
                    mirrors horizontally on the top edge too, so its lean stays
                    parallel across a section's two edges.
    h_scales      - the scale-step list (the caller already has it split).

  An unknown key falls through the `case` with an empty body and renders
  nothing, exactly as the canvas does for a mask it can't resolve.
{%- endcomment -%}

